# BEYOND RELICS — MASTER PROMPT FOR AI WEBSITE BUILDER

## 0. ROLE AND NON-NEGOTIABLE RULES

You are a senior product designer and front-end engineer. Build a complete, multi-page, production-quality website for an educational project called BEYOND RELICS. Follow every instruction in this prompt. Do not simplify, merge sections, or skip features. When something is ambiguous, choose the option that gives the most polished, credible and scientifically responsible result.

Non-negotiable rules:
1. The project name is BEYOND RELICS. The main character is COSMO. Never rename either.
2. The interface (backgrounds, text, buttons, borders, gradients, glows, icons, badges, overlays) uses only the palette defined in Section 3: dark space black, navy, electric blue, cyan and ice white. NO purple, violet or magenta may be used in any interface element. Exception: real space and science photographs (nebulae, galaxies, etc.) keep their natural colors, including purple and pink hues.
3. Never invent scientific facts, numbers, dates, discoveries, quotes or sources. If a fact cannot be supported by a source, leave it out (rules in Section 8).
4. Every button, link, tab and control must work. No decorative or dead UI.
5. Never generate, redraw or substitute the character COSMO. Use only the reference images the team uploads. Until then, use clearly labeled placeholder frames.
6. The comic content must be data-driven, so new chapters and pages can be added without touching components or redesigning anything.
7. Do not add a database, backend or login system. Reading progress, quiz results and badges are stored locally in the visitor's browser.

---

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

BEYOND RELICS is an educational scientific comic and interactive space exploration platform. It simplifies science and space topics through a comic book whose hero is COSMO, a fictional alien explorer. The project is entered in the NASA Space Apps Challenge.

It combines four things:
- Comic storytelling
- Astronomy and space exploration
- Reliable, sourced scientific knowledge
- Interactive learning

Goal: turn complex scientific information into a beautiful, enjoyable, easy-to-understand visual experience, especially for students and young people.

Audience: students, teenagers, young adults, teachers, and curious general readers. A competition jury will also evaluate the site, so it must look credible, polished and purposeful.

---

## 2. EXPERIENCE VISION AND DESIGN PRINCIPLES

This is NOT a gallery of comic images and NOT a generic landing page. It is a complete digital platform. The visitor should feel they are entering a space-science observatory and joining a scientific expedition led by COSMO.

The site blends three things:
- The credibility and clarity of an advanced space-science website
- The immersion of a premium digital comic reader
- Gentle, meaningful educational interaction

Design principles:
- Cinematic but calm. Premium, not flashy.
- Clear visual hierarchy. Every screen has one obvious focal point.
- Generous negative space. Never crowded.
- Scientific credibility first. Story and real science are always visually distinguishable.
- Motion adds depth, never distraction.

Avoid:
- A video-game look: no HUD clutter, no neon overload, no arcade fonts, no gamified chrome.
- Childish or cartoonish UI chrome around the comic. The comic art carries the playfulness; the interface stays refined.
- Template-looking sections. Do not produce a generic SaaS landing page layout.

