## 3. VISUAL IDENTITY

### 3.1 Color system (define as design tokens / CSS variables)
- Deep Space Black: #05080D (page background, reader stage)
- Midnight Navy: #0A1626 (surfaces, cards, header on scroll)
- Dark Blue: #102A43 (raised surfaces, borders, hover fills)
- Electric Blue: #1677FF (primary actions, active states, links)
- Cyan: #35D5F2 (accents, highlights, glow, focus rings, science markers)
- Ice White: #EAF4FF (primary text, icons)
- Derived tones are allowed only as lighter/darker or lower-opacity versions of the colors above (for example, Ice White at 70% for secondary text, Cyan at 15% for borders).
- Gradients only between black, navy, dark blue, electric blue and cyan.
- Glow effects use Electric Blue or Cyan at low opacity. Keep them subtle and elegant.
- Real photographs keep their natural colors. Purple and pink tones inside nebula, galaxy and other space photographs are allowed. Do not recolor, tint or color-grade photos to remove them. Only interface-level elements must be purple-free: never create purple gradients, glows or tinted overlays, and use dark navy or black overlays for text legibility on top of photos..
- Text contrast must meet WCAG AA at minimum.

### 3.2 Typography
- Display and headings: Space Grotesk (fallback: Sora, system sans-serif).
- Body: Inter.
- Small technical labels, captions, page counters and data tags: IBM Plex Mono, used sparingly.
- Do NOT use sci-fi display fonts such as Orbitron or Audiowide.
- Define a clear type scale: hero display, H1, H2, H3, body large, body, caption, label. Use tight tracking and uppercase on small labels only. Body line-height 1.6 or more, readable line length (about 60-75 characters) for long text.

### 3.3 Backgrounds and atmosphere
- Layered backgrounds: deep black base, soft navy-to-blue gradient glows, a fine star field, and very faint blue/cyan nebula haze.
- Star field must be lightweight (CSS or a small canvas). Reduce or freeze it on mobile and when the user prefers reduced motion.
- Add a gentle vignette so text always stays legible over imagery.
- Use cinematic imagery (planets, nebulae, galaxies) as large hero/section backdrops with dark gradient overlays for text contrast.

### 3.4 Components
- Primary button: solid Electric Blue, Ice White text, soft cyan outer glow on hover/focus, subtle 2px upward movement. Rounded (10-12px).
- Secondary button: transparent with a 1px Cyan or Ice White border, fills with Dark Blue on hover.
- Cards: Midnight Navy surface, 1px border (Cyan at about 12-18% opacity), 16px radius, faint inner glow, gentle lift and border brighten on hover.
- Chips and labels: small, uppercase, mono, thin border.
- Inputs: dark surface, cyan focus ring.
- Dividers: thin hairlines, optionally with small star-chart tick marks, very subtle.
- Icons: a single thin-stroke icon set (Lucide), consistent size and weight.
- Create a simple, elegant BEYOND RELICS wordmark (typographic, optionally with a minimal orbit-ring mark in SVG). Use it in header, footer and favicon.

### 3.5 Motion
- Durations 200-450ms, ease-out. Animate only transform and opacity.
- Scroll reveals: fade and rise of 12-24px, staggered lightly. Subtle parallax (maximum about 8%) on hero layers.
- Page transitions: short fade.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion everywhere (disable parallax, reveals become instant, star field static).
- No auto-playing loops that compete with reading. Nothing flashes.

### 3.6 Layout
- 8px spacing grid. 12-column desktop grid, content max width about 1200-1280px.
- Generous vertical rhythm between sections. Consistent section padding across all pages.

