## 7. CHARACTER AND IMAGE ASSET SYSTEM

- COSMO is the project's fixed character. The team will upload original reference images and comic pages. Use them exactly as provided. Never redraw, restyle, regenerate or replace COSMO, and never pick a substitute alien character.
- Until real files are provided, show clearly labeled placeholder frames ("COSMO — upload reference image here") that are the same size and position as the final images, so the layout does not change when they are swapped in.
- Organize assets in a clear structure: /public/characters/cosmo/, /public/comic/chapter-01/, /public/comic/chapter-02/, /public/science/, /public/explore/, /public/badges/. Comic page files use predictable names such as page-001.webp.
- Every image is referenced from the data files, not hardcoded in components, so replacing a placeholder means replacing a file or one data field.
- Every image has descriptive alt text and, where applicable, a credit line.
- For non-character imagery, use high-quality real space and science photography with cinematic framing. Use only images that can be legally used and credited (for example NASA imagery, following NASA media usage guidelines). Do not imply NASA endorsement. Credit every image.
- Provide hero, card and gallery images in several sizes (responsive srcset), with lazy loading and blur-up or skeleton placeholders. Preserve the original resolution of comic pages for the reader; do not over-compress them.

