## 9. TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS

Recommended stack (adapt to the platform if needed):
- React with TypeScript and Vite, Tailwind CSS (design tokens in the theme/CSS variables), React Router, Framer Motion (or CSS animations), Lucide icons. If the platform defaults to Next.js, use the App Router with static generation and keep the same structure.
- No backend, no database, no authentication.

Architecture:
- Component-based and modular. Reusable UI components: Button, Card, Chip, Badge, SectionHeader, ImageWithCredit, Modal/Drawer/BottomSheet, Toast, ProgressBar, Tabs, plus feature components such as ComicReader, PageThumbnailStrip, ScienceLinkPanel, QuizPlayer, TopicCard, MissionLogDrawer.
- All content in typed data files under src/data: comic (chapters and pages), science entries, explore topics, quizzes, badges, team, sources and image credits.
- Comic data fields: chapter id, slug, number, title, subtitle, cover image, and an ordered list of pages. Each page has an image path, alt text, and an optional list of science links (entry slug, label, optional marker position as percentages).
- Science entry fields: slug, title, topic, summary, story moment text, real science text, related chapter/page, images with credits, Did You Know fact, sources, related entries.
- Quiz fields: chapter id, questions with options, correct answer, explanation, related science entry.
- A small, documented progress store (local only) that exposes read and update helpers to components.
- Short README: how to run, project structure, how to add pages, chapters, science entries, quizzes and badges, how to replace placeholder images, and how to update team and sources.

Performance:
- Fast first load. Code-split routes, lazy-load heavy components and below-the-fold images, optimized WebP/AVIF assets, responsive srcset, explicit image dimensions to avoid layout shift, font preloading with display swap and limited font weights.
- Animate only transform and opacity. Keep the star field lightweight. Target Lighthouse scores of 90 or more for Performance and 95 or more for Accessibility, Best Practices and SEO.

Responsive:
- Fully responsive from 360px phones to large desktop screens (breakpoints around 640, 768, 1024, 1280, 1536). Touch targets at least 44px. Test the reader in portrait and landscape. No horizontal scrolling on any page.

Accessibility:
- Semantic HTML landmarks, one H1 per page, logical heading order, full keyboard navigation, visible focus rings (cyan), focus trapping in drawers and modals, aria labels on icon buttons, aria-live for reader page changes and quiz feedback, alt text on all meaningful images, WCAG AA contrast, reduced-motion support.

SEO fundamentals:
- Unique title and meta description per route, Open Graph and Twitter tags with a social image slot, canonical URLs, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, descriptive link text, structured heading hierarchy, fast loading.

Browser support: latest Chrome, Safari, Firefox and Edge, plus iOS Safari and Android Chrome.

Code quality: clean, consistent naming, no dead code, no console errors or warnings, no unused dependencies, comments only where logic is non-obvious.

